                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Spent about 45 minutes in the game, cleared the first couple of worlds. It has a neat idea, but it lacks in overall execution. The fairy you warp to is controlled by the second joystick (in a very awkward manner that often leads my thumb to falling off the joystick) or with the arrow keys, neither of which feel like particularly well-tuned control schemes if consistent control is what is desired. I would have preferred mouse-controls if possible. \n\nFurthermore, the warp button is finnicky. Many times I will have more than enough meter to warp, but it just won't let me. When warping is about the only thing you really do 90% of the time, it really needs to be fine tuned and it just isn't in this game. \n\nLastly, the biggest problem is...this game really isn't that much fun. The mechanics are shallow and the level design is even more so. Interaction is minimal, so having a mindless, repetitive game in which your one mechanic (which doesnt even work some times) does not a fun game make.\n\nIf this game was 3-5$ I could see it maybe being passable, but I have gotten far more enjoyment out of many other games at that price point, let alone 10$. There's an idea here, but it really needs to be fleshed out more to make the game fun.",
